CAVEAT:  Proven with one receiver on one segment and a static two-router topology. The
         SSM range tested in anger is the IANA default 232/8; `ip pim ssm range <acl>`
         was exercised only far enough to establish finding F-14 (STEP 5), and its
         dataplane behaviour beyond "nothing leaks" was not characterised. Removal of
         the SSM range cannot be shown in the dataplane on 232/8 at all, for the reason
         given in STEP 5, so removal is proven by an admission test rather than by a
         drop to zero. swi_a was configured but never reloaded or power-cycled, so
         reboot persistence is proven for the DUT only.

