  tools   : tools/igmp.py on tb277 sends the joins and leaves. PIM-SSM is DEFINED by the
            (S,G) join and IGMPv2 cannot carry a source list, so the subject of this
            case could not be expressed with what the bench had; igmp.py was extended
            with an IGMPv3 mode for it -- `-3`, `--source A[,B]`, `--record
            {is-include|is-exclude|to-include|to-exclude|allow|block}`, defaulting to
            `to-include` on join (what a real host sends when it joins an SSM channel)
            and to `to-include` with an EMPTY source list on leave (how IGMPv3 leaves an
            include-mode group). Reports go to 224.0.0.22; the tool picks the right
            destination and link-layer address for each version. tools/arpleg.py drives
            every counted leg; its per-spec source override `--udp DST:PORT@SRC` is what
