  Authored expected result, verbatim: "Multicast routing table updates accordingly"

  Method: "port interface" is ambiguous on a two-router bench, so BOTH readings were
  taken, because they differ. The channel was re-joined and forwarding re-confirmed
  first (cap s6-rejoin-eth4.pcap: 9/10 channel + 10/10 instrument control).

  (a) the RECEIVER'S PORT down -- DUT port1.0.48, the host's own access port:

awplus(config-if)#shutdown
awplus#show interface port1.0.48 status
  port1.0.48 ... disabled
swi_a#show ip igmp groups
232.5.5.5        vlan48               00:00:45  stopped 10.38.22.70   <-- STILL THERE
swi_a#show ip mroute
(10.38.22.40, 232.5.5.5) ... Incoming interface: vlan61
  Outgoing interface list: vlan48 (1)                                 <-- STILL THERE

      The multicast table does NOT update, and that is correct rather than a fault. The
      reason is the topology: port1.0.48 is an L2 access port ON THE DUT, while the
      multicast router is swi_a, whose vlan48 SVI is still up over the trunk. swi_a has
      no way to learn that a host two switches away unplugged, and the membership is
      soft state that must time out. It is recorded because a tester who shuts the
      host's port and expects the table to clear will record a false failure (O-28).
      `no shutdown` restored it: `port1.0.48 ... connected a-full a-1000`.

  (b) the ROUTER'S INTERFACE down -- swi_a `interface vlan48`, the multicast interface:

swi_a(config-if)#shutdown
swi_a#show ip igmp groups
  (header only; empty)
swi_a#show ip mroute
IP Multicast Routing Table
